# Package Gate Example

Copy this file to `.agent/package_gate.md` only for local runs. The live file is
ignored and must not be committed.

When a new package starts, refresh the live gate so the active package and unit
match the current approved work. Stale active-package references are a stop
condition.

## Package

Package 11 - Final public polish and closeout

## Active unit

Package 11A - Docs-only public polish and closeout

## Package-level exit gate

Package 11 is complete only when:

- Package 10 is already committed.
- The README gives a clear first-pass portfolio narrative.
- `docs/demo_walkthrough.md` explains the local command path, expected ignored
  artefacts, key tables, safe SQL inspection, Package 10 interpretation,
  troubleshooting, and synthetic-data honesty.
- `docs/project_closeout.md` records the final boundary, checklist, local
  artefacts that remain uncommitted, and stop conditions.
- `docs/packages.md`, `docs/runbook.md`, and `docs/decisions.md` align on the
  docs-only Package 11 scope.
- `docs/gtm_policy.md` remains unchanged as the Package 10 source of truth.
- No code, tests, Make targets, generated outputs, DuckDB tables, model logic,
  scoring logic, observability logic, or new GTM policy logic are added.
- No generated outputs, DuckDB files, MLflow runs, cache folders, live `.agent`
  files, private files, or local-only artefacts are tracked.
- `make public-safety-check` passes.
- `git diff --check` passes.
- `git status --short` is reviewed.

## Stop conditions

Stop before making any change that would:

- Start Package 11 while Package 10 is uncommitted.
- Change the locked `gtm_policy_v1` matrix, thresholds, exact strings, or
  boundary rules without an explicit durable-doc decision/update.
- Add new code or product behavior instead of docs-only closeout work.
- Use real customer or company data.
- Add dashboards, APIs, cloud deployment, CRM integration, campaign execution,
  or screenshots pretending to be a real production UI.
- Claim real-world commercial validation from synthetic outputs.
- Weaken public-repo security.
- Commit generated artefacts.
- Commit live local `.agent/*.md` files.
- Add unapproved production dependencies.
- Expand Package 11 beyond public documentation and closeout.
